('sherman-oaks', 'Los Angeles Department of Water and Power', 'Los Angeles Department of Building and Safety', 'Sherman Oaks projects are typically reviewed through Los Angeles city permitting, with LADWP coordination important for EV chargers, panel upgrades, hillside homes, and commercial electrical work.', 'Sherman Oaks includes single family homes, hillside properties, apartments, condos, offices, retail spaces, and restaurants with varied electrical loads and parking layouts.', 'Garages, hillside driveways, multifamily parking, and commercial lots can affect EV charger placement, conduit routing, and panel capacity.', 'Ventura Boulevard commercial spaces, offices, restaurants, retail, and multifamily buildings commonly need lighting, dedicated circuits, panel service, and EV charging planning.'),
('silver-lake', 'Los Angeles Department of Water and Power', 'Los Angeles Department of Building and Safety', 'Silver Lake projects are usually reviewed through Los Angeles city permitting, with LADWP coordination important for hillside homes, older panels, multifamily buildings, and EV charging work.', 'Silver Lake includes hillside homes, older houses, duplexes, apartments, creative offices, and retail spaces where access, grounding, and load capacity need review.', 'Steep driveways, detached garages, shared parking, and narrow access can affect EV charger location and conduit routing.', 'Local commercial work commonly includes lighting, dedicated circuits, panel repair, troubleshooting, small tenant improvements, and EV charging feasibility.'),
('torrance', 'Southern California Edison', 'City of Torrance Community Development', 'Torrance projects commonly require city permit coordination and SCE capacity review for EV charging, panel work, industrial electrical loads, and commercial improvements.', 'Torrance includes single family homes, apartments, retail centers, medical offices, warehouses, industrial properties, and larger parking areas where electrical planning matters.', 'Garages, commercial lots, fleet parking, warehouse parking, and multifamily stalls can affect charger placement, load management, and routing.', 'Industrial, retail, medical, office, warehouse, and multifamily properties commonly need dedicated circuits, lighting, panel service, troubleshooting, and EV charging infrastructure.'),
('venice', 'Los Angeles Department of Water and Power', 'Los Angeles Department of Building and Safety', 'Venice projects are typically reviewed through Los Angeles city permitting, with LADWP service review important for coastal homes, multifamily parking, retail spaces, and EV charging work.', 'Venice includes coastal homes, duplexes, multifamily buildings, retail storefronts, restaurants, offices, and properties with tight access or exterior exposure.', 'Carports, narrow lots, alley access, coastal exposure, shared parking, and detached structures can affect charger placement and conduit routing.', 'Retail, restaurant, office, hospitality, and multifamily spaces commonly need lighting, dedicated circuits, panel service, troubleshooting, and EV charging planning.'),
